Subject: src/diff.c: on OpenVMS, end main with exit()

diff returns its status from main.  On VMS exit() goes through
vms_exit() (lib/stdlib.h, patch 0004), which gives DCL a status of the
right severity (success, warning for "files differ", error for trouble);
a return from main does not, so a missing file looked like success.

--- a/src/diff.c	2026-10-05 04:07:48.969906533 +0100
+++ b/src/diff.c	2026-10-05 04:08:04.980247841 +0100
@@ -889,7 +889,13 @@
 
   check_stdout ();
   cleanup_signal_handlers ();
+#ifdef __VMS
+  /* exit (lib/stdlib.h) gives DCL a status of the right severity; a
+     return from main would not.  */
+  exit (exit_status);
+#else
   return exit_status;
+#endif
 }
 
